---
import CortexLegalLayout from '../../layouts/CortexLegalLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY, getApp } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('cortex')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 23, 2026';
const supportVersion = '1.1';
const title = `${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`;
const description =
  'Help with Cortex on iPhone, including local game data, private iCloud Sudoku sync, optional Game Center, widgets, resets, and pre-release availability.';
---

<CortexLegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/cortex/support"
  page="support"
  heading="Cortex Support"
  documentMeta={`Version ${supportVersion} · Updated ${updatedDate}`}
  summary="Cortex 1.1 (21) is an iPhone-only internal TestFlight build for iOS 18 or later. External beta and App Store availability are not public."
>
  <div class="cx-legal-layout">
    <nav class="cx-legal-toc" aria-label="Support sections">
      <strong>On this page</strong>
      <a href="#availability">Availability</a>
      <a href="#launch">Launch problems</a>
      <a href="#local-data">Local data</a>
      <a href="#icloud">iCloud Sudoku sync</a>
      <a href="#game-center">Game Center</a>
      <a href="#widgets">Widgets</a>
      <a href="#reset">Reset or reinstall</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="cx-legal-copy">
      <section id="availability" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Current availability</h2>
        <p class="cx-legal-callout">
          Cortex 1.1 (21) is VALID, attached, and available through internal
          TestFlight for iPhone. The app target supports iOS 18 or later. Cortex
          does not support iPad, and external beta or App Store availability is not
          public.
        </p>
        <p>
          Distribution work may change independently of this page. This page does
          not promise a release date, public beta, or acquisition access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="launch" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>If Cortex will not launch</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Confirm the iPhone is running iOS 18 or later.</li>
          <li>
            If a private build was provided to your Apple Account, install the
            newest build available through the channel named in that invitation.
          </li>
          <li>Force-quit Cortex, reopen it, and restart the iPhone if needed.</li>
          <li>
            Check that the iPhone has free storage and that Apple’s distribution
            service is available.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Avoid deleting Cortex as an early troubleshooting step if the iPhone may
          contain the only copy of game progress or statistics you care about.
          Most Cortex data has no Nintek server backup.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="local-data" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Local progress, settings, and statistics</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex stores game progress, active runs, settings, records, and detailed
          statistics on the iPhone. If a game does not resume or a statistic looks
          stale, return to the Cortex hub, reopen the game, and complete a new
          result before restarting the app. Include the game name and what changed
          when contacting support.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cortex has no custom account, Nintek gameplay server, or complete cloud
          backup. Nintek cannot retrieve or rebuild local data from a backend.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="icloud" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Troubleshoot private iCloud Sudoku sync</h2>
        <p>
          Only Sudoku statistics use Apple’s private iCloud key-value storage.
          Other game progress and active runs should not be expected to sync.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Confirm the iPhone is signed in to the intended Apple Account and is
            online.
          </li>
          <li>
            In Apple Settings, confirm iCloud is available and Cortex is allowed to
            use iCloud when it appears in the app list.
          </li>
          <li>
            Open Cortex on each relevant iPhone and allow Apple time to deliver
            key-value changes; sync timing is controlled by iCloud.
          </li>
          <li>
            Check Apple’s system status if a recent change has not appeared.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Nintek cannot inspect, merge, force, or restore the private iCloud store.
          Do not delete the app while troubleshooting if an iPhone may hold the
          only local copy you want to keep.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118225">
            Apple: change which apps sync and store data with iCloud
          </a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/support/systemstatus/">
            Apple System Status
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="game-center" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Troubleshoot optional Game Center</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex works without Game Center. To use Apple-managed player identity,
          scores, leaderboards, and achievements, confirm Game Center is enabled
          and signed in under Apple Settings. Reopen Cortex after changing that
          setting and connect to the internet so pending reports can retry.
        </p>
        <p>
          Apple controls authentication, player profiles, leaderboard records, and
          achievement records. Nintek cannot reset a Game Center profile, change an
          Apple Account, or delete Apple-held records.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/iphone/set-up-your-game-center-profile-iphd26b2beaa/ios">
            Apple: set up and manage a Game Center profile
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="widgets" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Troubleshoot Quick Launch and Stats widgets</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Open Cortex once after installing or updating it, then play or finish a
            game so Cortex can write a fresh App Group snapshot.
          </li>
          <li>
            For Quick Launch, edit the widget and confirm the intended Cortex game
            is selected.
          </li>
          <li>
            If Stats remains stale, open Cortex, return to the Home Screen, and
            allow iOS time to refresh the widget timeline.
          </li>
          <li>
            Remove and add the widget again if its configuration or snapshot still
            does not update.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Widget refresh timing is scheduled by iOS. Removing a widget does not
          erase Cortex’s local game data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="reset" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Resetting a game or reinstalling Cortex</h2>
        <p>
          A game’s restart or reset action starts that board or run again. It does
          not erase all Cortex history, settings, aggregate statistics, widget
          data, iCloud data, or Game Center records.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cortex currently has no single in-app erase-all control. Deleting and
          reinstalling the app is the complete on-device reset, and removes local
          app and App Group data from that iPhone. That data cannot be recovered
          from a Nintek server. Private iCloud Sudoku statistics may return after
          reinstalling, and Apple-held Game Center scores and achievements remain
          associated with the Apple service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Read the <a href={app.privacyPath}>Cortex Privacy Policy</a> for details
          about local storage, private iCloud Sudoku statistics, App Group widget
          snapshots, optional Game Center, permissions, retention, and deletion.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="credits" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Third-party credits and content provenance</h2>
        <p>
          From the Cortex hub, open <strong>Content &amp; Provenance</strong> to
          review and export the canonical notices and source ledger. They cover
          the retained ENABLE-derived Wordfoundry corpus and first-party or
          owner-attested visual sources, including six owner-generated
          GPT-Image-2 sheets. Former OpenMoji-derived content was removed and does
          not ship in the current remediation build.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090122025747/http://personal.riverusers.com/~thegrendel/software.html">
              Archived ENABLE project source
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use/">
              OpenAI Terms of Use cited by the provenance record
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Contact Cortex support</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the
          iPhone model, iOS version, Cortex version or TestFlight build number, the
          affected game or feature, and the steps that led to the problem. Include
          a screenshot only if you are comfortable sharing what it contains.
        </p>
        <p>
          Do not send your Apple Account password, verification codes, payment
          information, or other credentials. For privacy questions, email
          <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
          Use of Cortex is subject to the
          <a href={app.termsPath}>Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</CortexLegalLayout>
